// A call among data that holds a function, in a block whose tail is that
// data's name: the binding the fuzzer wraps a program in is generic, and
// the call's cells were swept into its scheme, so the callback's instance
// had no types of its own (soak nov24f, the check accepted what the build
// refused: "an instance at fn(x: _) -> _ of a definition typed fn(s:
// string) -> string"; six findings on one box).
// Expected trace (both engines): the pair, its function printed.
{ let f = (array::map(["a", "bb"], |s| s), |z| z); f }
